1. Open browser.
2. Search Microsoft Sysinternals TCPView.
3. Download TCPView from Microsoft.
4. Extract ZIP file.
5. Open TCPView.
6. Run as Administrator if required.
7. Observe columns:

Process - Application name
PID - Process ID
Protocol - TCP / UDP
Local Address - Your system address
Local Port - Local port
Remote Address - Destination address
Remote Port - Destination port
State - Connection status

8. Select any active connection.
9. Note process, PID, protocol, local and remote endpoints.
10. Right-click connection for available options.

COMMAND PROMPT:
netstat -ano

11. Match PID with Task Manager:
    Ctrl + Shift + Esc > Details > PID.

NOTE:
- TCP has connection states.
- UDP usually does not show TCP states.
